{
 "_note": "DATA: weekday peak-hour turning-movement counts at intersections in the model area, transcribed from the traffic appendices of two certified environmental impact reports (public documents of the City of Oakland). Volumes are vehicles per hour by approach (SB arrives on the N leg, WB on the E leg, NB on the S leg, EB on the W leg) and movement (L left, T through, R right, U U-turn), for the peak hour of each intersection. Leg bearings (from the intersection toward the leg) and coordinates are read from OpenStreetMap geometry and only serve to place each leg on the network. Provenance and method: data/demand/README.md, \"Seventeenth round\". No growth factor is applied (ASSUMPTION).",
 "sources": {
  "CHRCO-EIR2014": {
   "citation": "[CHRCO-EIR2014]",
   "document": "Children's Hospital and Research Center Oakland Campus Master Plan Project, Draft Environmental Impact Report (LSA Associates for the City of Oakland, August 2014, SCH 2013072058), Appendix C, transportation data: intersection count sheets (Thursday 2013-09-19, 7 to 9 AM and 3 to 6 PM, All Traffic Data Services) and Synchro worksheets by Fehr & Peers",
   "url": "https://www.oaklandca.gov/files/assets/city/v/1/planning-amp-building/documents/dp/ceqa/2011-present/childrens-hospital-draft-environmental-impact-report-appendix-c.pdf",
   "counts": "Peak-hour totals of the count sheets (AM from 8:00; PM from 16:45 or 17:00, each intersection its own peak hour)."
  },
  "SafewayCollege-DEIR2011": {
   "citation": "[SafewayCollege-DEIR2011]",
   "document": "Safeway Shopping Center, College and Claremont Avenues, Draft Environmental Impact Report (City of Oakland, July 2011, SCH 2009112008), Appendix: traffic count sheets (Tuesday 2010-03-16, 4 to 7 PM, peak hour from 5:15 PM, National Data & Surveying Services) and Synchro worksheets by Fehr & Peers",
   "url": "https://www.oaklandca.gov/files/assets/city/v/1/planning-amp-building/documents/dp/ceqa/2011-present/college-avenue-safeway-deir_2024-05-10-203917_bvqg.pdf",
   "counts": "Volumes of the \"Existing PM Peak Hour\" worksheets: the counts, plus the vehicles left in queue at the end of the hour on the approaches the report names (Ashby Ave and Claremont Ave eastbound; Alcatraz Ave and College Ave northbound and southbound), so they are demand volumes. No AM count exists."
  }
 },
